---
/**
 * Where an ambient-motion effect layer goes (BL-035, ADR-0039): the homepage
 * hero (Hero's `backdrop` slot) and the /brand preview stage.
 *
 * An empty placeholder. The layer itself is built in the browser by
 * src/scripts/ambient/runtime.ts, which only a browser that draws motion ever
 * loads (src/scripts/ambient/loader.ts), after the page has loaded; it fades
 * in. Motion is on by default; a browser that switched it off, or prefers
 * reduced motion, gets this one empty div.
 *
 * What must hold before any script runs stays here: the box fills its
 * nearest positioned ancestor and never takes part in layout, so filling it
 * later cannot shift anything, and reduced motion hides it. The parent must be
 * `position: relative`; content that should sit above the layer needs its own
 * stacking (the global `.container` rule already has it).
 */
---

<div class="ambient" data-ambient-mount aria-hidden="true"></div>

<style>
  .ambient {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* Reduced motion wins over any stored choice: the layer is not drawn at all. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .ambient {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
